1. Trend Tracking Indicators
    200-Day SMA: Defines long-term bull or bear market regimes.
    50-Day EMA: Identifies structural, medium-term trend direction and support.
    20-Day EMA: Tracks short-term swing momentum on daily charts.
    MACD: Measures trend changes via moving average convergence/divergence.
    Supertrend: Uses ATR variations to signal clear trend reversals.

2. Momentum & Overbought/Oversold Oscillators
    14-Day RSI: Spotlights daily overextended levels above 70 or below 30.
    Stochastic: Tracks closing prices relative to high-low ranges for turns.
    CCI: Measures price deviations from statistical means to find cycles.
    Rate of Change: Calculates percentage velocity of daily price movements.
    Money Flow Index: Combines price and volume to gauge momentum strength.

3. Volatility & Channel Indicators
    Bollinger Bands: Visualizes daily volatility expansion and contraction cycles.
    Keltner Channels: Uses ATR bands around an EMA to identify breakouts.
    Donchian Channels: Maps highest highs and lowest lows over set periods.
    ATR (14-Day): Displays average daily trading range in absolute points.

4. Volume & Liquidity Tools
    Volume (Daily): Confirms institutional participation on breakout or breakdown days.
    Volume Profile: Displays price levels where highest daily volume accumulated.
    OBV: Tracks cumulative volume flow to anticipate major trend changes.
    Chaikin Money Flow: Evaluates institutional accumulation or distribution pressures.

5. Multi-Variable & Structural Overlay Systems
    Ichimoku Cloud: Provides complete support, resistance, and trend-direction layers.
    Parabolic SAR: Places daily trailing stop dots to maximize trend capture.



